WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.520
It really pains me to have to talk about this
today.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.270
It really does.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.750
But I'm really worried about a faction of
my audience and, and quite frankly, I'm really

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.809
worried about the left and this is not concerned
trolling.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:20.220
I'm worried because of the response to a video
that I did yesterday explaining some unfortunate

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.029
realities about Medicare for all.

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:28.509
I did a video yesterday where I explained
in no uncertain terms, we're not getting Medicare

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:30.800
for all anytime soon.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.960
Now there are lots of good progressive takes
that agree with that.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.329
One example is a progressive economists, Dean
Baker's recent comments about Medicare for

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:41.760
all he, he is a progressive.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.820
I had him on the show recently.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.440
There was no question about it.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.859
I did the video in good faith.

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:48.699
I said, listen, I'm for Medicare for all.

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:50.630
I believe Medicare for all is the gold standard.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.359
I want Medicare for all.

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:56.980
I'm not suggesting that we push lame centrist
policy because getting Medicare for all will

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.050
take much longer than some people think.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.519
I'm not suggesting that we don't hold our
candidates accountable to the gold standard.

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:05.350
That is Medicare for all.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:10.250
But I explained to some unfortunate realities
about Medicare for all with the hope that

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:17.149
once we all understand these, we can be stronger
in our advocacy for better policy as activists,

00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:20.910
as media people, as voters, people in the
audience.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.860
The video I did is about 10 minutes long and
I expected that there would be some comments

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.719
and David, you're kind of being a defeatist
here even though it's not what I'm, what I'm

00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:30.829
actually doing.

00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:36.170
Uh, but the reaction has been, um, again,
it's just from a piece of my audience.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.390
A lot of people understood what I was doing
and appreciated it.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.380
Three minutes after the video was published.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.780
Remember the video is 10 minutes long, three
minutes after the video was published.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.060
It had 50 dislikes.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.290
It's only been three minutes.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.009
You couldn't possibly have watched the 10
minute video.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:54.560
Even if you had it on double time on YouTube
in the three minutes it took 50 people to

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.560
dislike the video.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.939
And there are either people who didn't watch
the video at all or people who just watched

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:06.140
it and don't understand what I'm saying or
people making bad faith arguments.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:12.510
But I am very worried because if that is the
contingent that the success of our movement

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.360
depends on, we will lose.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.360
And I hate to say that.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:22.300
Let me give you some examples and um, uh,
again I'm doing this because I want to win

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:28.210
and I'm worried that there are factions in
our movement that are totally misguided and

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.740
their reactions to, to, to people simply saying,
Hey guys, we should be aware of this stuff.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.800
One example, I'm not surprised David is shilling
against Medicare.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:43.720
I actually say in the video probably close
to a dozen times I am for Medicare for all

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.050
this is either an ignorant or a bad faith
comment.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:52.750
Another user responded, Bernie can establish
a state of emergency and sign it into law.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.930
Trump has set so many precedents.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:03:00.610
Listen, this is where the the the, there is
an element of the left that is in a fantasy

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.610
world.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:07.400
We are not going to get Medicare for all established
through a presidential state of emergency.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:13.070
I understand that there's some hypothetical
world in which president Bernie Sanders says,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:18.910
our uh, healthcare situation is so bad that
I'm declaring a state of emergency and during

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:24.180
that state of emergency I am going to simply
create Medicare for all and then boom, we

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.910
will have Medicare for all.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:26.910
It's just unrealistic.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:27.910
Okay?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.530
It's not worth even putting energy into that
and responding to what I'm talking about by

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.580
saying, David, Bernie will just declare a
state of emergency and create Medicare for

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.580
all.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.580
It's not happening.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.810
We are not going to win if that's what we
are hoping for or waiting for.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.830
Another example, this was a very bad take
and a bad faith argument.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:44.830
David [inaudible].

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:45.890
What was bad faith about it?

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.300
They don't say, this sounds like a Nancy Pelosi
speech.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.930
Please go back to being more progressive.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.060
People liked you more that way.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.310
I mean, listen, the show is bigger than ever.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.120
It's more than doubled in the last year, but
that's not really the, actually don't think

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.120
that's the issue.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.960
That doesn't tell us whether I'm right or
wrong.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:04.980
The idea that it's a bad faith argument when
I'm saying I'm for Medicare for all, we should

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.290
still push for Medicare for all.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.850
We should demand our candidates before Medicare
for all.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.890
That is what seems like bad faith to me.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.010
Uh, another comment.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.010
Okay.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:18.109
So David is basically advocating for centrist
policies so that we have a chance in the future.

00:04:18.109 --> 00:04:26.580
No, I literally say in the video, I am not
suggesting that we advocate for centrist policies.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.300
I say it in the video.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.900
So again, either people aren't listening or
they're making bad faith arguments.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:38.699
And lastly, now is the time to unsubscribe
from this channel.

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:40.830
Do this to be making a point.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.159
No progressive should ever be posting against
Medicare for all.

00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:48.620
So again, number one, I say a dozen times
in the video, I'm for Medicare for all.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:54.360
But more importantly, that is the sort of
black and white thinking, these these bogus

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.659
litmus tests that are not connected to reality.

00:04:57.659 --> 00:05:02.840
Not only am I for Medicare for all, I'm trying
to figure out the right way to get there.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:07.960
One idea I had is it's more likely to start
with a state doing Medicare for all.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.940
That was one example that I gave.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.849
Now, fortunately I did get some emails from
people who took the time to email me and say,

00:05:14.849 --> 00:05:18.259
David, I know you're going to get crap for
this, but you're right and I think it's good

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:19.259
that you're doing it.

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:22.870
We need to be more armed with facts so that
we can better advocate for what we want.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.150
There were a few YouTube comments that that
seemed to understand what was going on.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:29.590
One who said these comments show people don't
listen to what he's saying.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.590
Yeah.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.199
Another comment or who said the comments are
depressing.

00:05:32.199 --> 00:05:33.199
Watch the whole video.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.730
He supports Medicare for all.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.800
He's talking about strategy here.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.020
He's talking about reality.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.020
He's right.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.919
He's saying it because people need to know
the reality.

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:45.879
We need realistic expectations and knowledge
about how the system works, so listen, I'm

00:05:45.879 --> 00:05:48.400
not being, I'm not acting in bad faith.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.590
I'm saying a Bernie presidency doesn't get
it for us, for all of the reasons that I cited

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:55.789
yesterday and more I want it.

00:05:55.789 --> 00:05:57.249
I think it's the best.

00:05:57.249 --> 00:05:58.319
Listen to what I'm saying.

00:05:58.319 --> 00:05:59.770
It's not impossible.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:06.310
It's just way more work and we need to know
that going in and we aren't going to succeed

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.319
in any of this.

00:06:07.319 --> 00:06:13.259
If we imagine such delusional things, as Bernie
will say, we have an emergency and put in

00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:15.750
Medicare for all, it's not going to happen.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:16.750
It's not going to happen.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:22.800
An any time wasted expecting that or suggesting
that is time that you are distracting from

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.069
doing the real work that needs to be done.

00:06:25.069 --> 00:06:26.069
Prove me wrong.

00:06:26.069 --> 00:06:27.069
I want to be wrong.

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:28.069
Okay?

00:06:28.069 --> 00:06:32.849
This is one of those things where if in three
years we have Medicare for all, I will gladly

00:06:32.849 --> 00:06:35.020
show up and say, you know what?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.150
I was skeptical but I was wrong.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:42.050
You all great activists prove me wrong and
we have Medicare for all.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:48.020
I hope that that happens, but it's not going
to be closer to a reality if the reaction

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:53.430
is David, you shouldn't even allude to the
fact that it might be more difficult than

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.169
some people are making it out to be.

00:06:55.169 --> 00:07:00.810
Spend the time advocating for a groundswell
of progressive candidates at all levels, all

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:05.659
of whom want Medicare for all so that we can
take back the white house and the Senate and

00:07:05.659 --> 00:07:09.539
governor's mansions and the Supreme court,
which will be crucial in actually getting

00:07:09.539 --> 00:07:11.820
working Medicare for all.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:18.360
But if the reason, uh, if the reaction to
me being realistic is, David, you're a shill.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.990
You're a bad person for doing this.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:24.050
You shouldn't be saying this, I'm now a right
winger or a centrist or whatever.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:30.569
We will lose if we attack people who agree
with us on policy, not because they even disagree

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:36.569
on one policy, but because they differently
assess its path to reality, they will crush

00:07:36.569 --> 00:07:37.569
us.

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:38.569
They will crush us.

00:07:38.569 --> 00:07:39.639
We will lose if that's what we do.

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:42.919
Mark my words, we will forget about Medicare
for all.

00:07:42.919 --> 00:07:44.360
Trump will get reelected.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.919
We will not get the Senate.

00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:48.960
It is upsetting to see, and I'll go even further.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:55.930
I've talked before about how our system is
set up to prevent people from really activating

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:59.879
what we really need are mass rallies in urban
centers.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:05.110
We need to consider strategic defaults to
cripple the financial system, mass work call-outs

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:08.819
to cripple industry, serious forms of protest.

00:08:08.819 --> 00:08:14.220
But as I've said before, the system is designed,
designed so that no one can afford to do that

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.800
by keeping wages stagnant, keeping public
transit terrible in most places.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.800
And the rest of it, we've talked about it
before.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.870
Let's work together because the reaction to
yesterday's video from this piece of my audience

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.129
is how we end up accomplishing nothing.

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:33.340
And I don't want to accomplish nothing.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.620
I am not suggesting we give up on anything.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.000
Should we fight for Medicare for all?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.110
Yes, we should.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:43.910
Should we always start negotiations from the
morally correct position that we actually

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:44.910
believe in?

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:49.690
Is Medicare for all of course, but responding
with kill the messenger too.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:54.270
I think some people are missing the reality
of how this becomes, uh, the law, how this

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.260
becomes our status quo.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:03.010
It's toxic and it will destroy the left, which
I don't want to see and I would actually argue

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:08.190
that the left has already been hurt by the
significantly on the positions we are already

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.110
with the majority of the country.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:14.840
Every poll tells us on healthcare, we are
with the majority on gun safety.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.320
We are with the majority.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.120
One of the reasons there are many reasons
and many of them are structural and know gerrymandering

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.110
and campaign finance.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:27.610
One of the reasons why we have not been more
effective is this infighting that exists.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.860
When someone says, Hey, I'm with you on everything
except I disagree about how easy you think

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.050
it's going to be and here's what we need to
know.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.410
We're going to lose, we're going to lose and
I don't want to lose.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.230
Tell me all the ways that I'm wrong.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.600
If you can actually keep it issue-based.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.350
I'm on Twitter at D Pacman.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.350
Leave a reply below.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:44.720
I'm sure that there will be more followup
about this upcoming,

